<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Privacy manifest for the MorkeTunnel iOS APPEX bundle (T-REL-9).
	     Separate from the app's (Config/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy) because a manifest describes
	     the bundle it ships in, and this bundle links different code.

	     Both categories below come from Frameworks/Libbox.xcframework, not from our
	     Swift/C/ObjC — which contains none of these APIs. The shipping ios-arm64 slice is a
	     STATIC archive ("current ar archive") carrying no manifest of its own, so libbox's
	     symbols become this bundle's to declare.
	     Re-measured 2026-11-14 (T-ARCH-43, engine v1.14.4-morke.1), after 2026-09-23 (T-REL-14(b),
	     v1.14.1-morke.1), both times on the LINKED Release
	     arm64 appex from an ARCHIVE (`xcodebuild archive … CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO
	     LD_GENERATE_MAP_FILE=YES`), read from its link map and `nm -u`: _stat _fstat _fstatat
	     _lstat _mach_absolute_time are imported, and nothing else on Apple's required-reason
	     list is — no statfs / statvfs / fstatfs / fstatvfs, no getattrlist family, no
	     NSFileSystem*/volume-capacity key, no UserDefaults, no activeInputModes, no systemUptime.
	     So FileTimestamp and SystemBootTime are declared and nothing else. The DiskSpace entry
	     this file carried since 2026-08-31 was measured on the untrimmed engine; its symbols left
	     with the T-ARCH-31 trim and are absent from the v1.13.13 archive as well.
	     v1.14 imports six symbols v1.13.13 did not — _mach_continuous_time _proc_pid_rusage
	     _sysctlbyname _notify_register_check _notify_check _notify_cancel — and none is on
	     Apple's list (bundleresources/…/nsprivacyaccessedapitype, read 2026-09-23), so none
	     adds a category. v1.14.4 changes the imports again (+ _dispatch_async __dispatch_main_q
	     _if_indextoname _notify_register_file_descriptor, the NSProcessInfo / NSThread / UIDevice
	     classes of sing-box's power report; − _notify_check _notify_register_check) and none of
	     those is on the list either, so the two categories below stand unchanged.

	     This file is a bundle RESOURCE, not a linked dependency: it adds nothing to what MorkeTunnel
	     links (MorkeShared and WidgetKit, T-EXT-1), and the NE memory budget is untouched. -->

	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>

	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>

	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!-- _stat _fstat _fstatat _lstat, from libbox — all four imported by the v1.14.1
			     archive (2026-09-23) and by the v1.14.4 archive (2026-11-14).
			     C617.1 is "metadata of files inside the app container, app group container, or
			     the app's CloudKit container". SingBoxTunnel.start puts every path libbox
			     touches inside the App Group container: basePath = container,
			     workingPath = container/Working, tempPath = container/Library/Caches, plus the
			     cache_file (cache.db) the config validator allow-lists — see
			     MorkeServices/VPN/TunnelWorkspace.swift, which wipes exactly those paths.
			     NOT DDA9.1 (no file timestamp is ever displayed), NOT 3B52.1 (no document
			     picker), NOT 0A2A.1 (third-party-SDK-only reason; this is the app's bundle). -->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>C617.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
		<dict>
			<!-- _mach_absolute_time, from libbox (imported by the v1.14.1 archive, 2026-09-23, and
			     the v1.14.4 archive, 2026-11-14):
			     Go's monotonic clock (runtime.nanotime, backing timers, deadlines and
			     time.Since) plus the vendored tracing library's clock.
			     35F9.1 is "measure the amount of time that has elapsed between events that
			     occurred within the app or to perform calculations to enable timers" — exactly
			     what a monotonic clock is used for here. Its "may not be sent off-device" clause
			     is satisfied by the project's privacy posture: no per-user analytics, no
			     behavioural tracking, no remote crash reporter, and the operational-health
			     metrics are os_log plus the on-device AnalyticsLedger files in the App Group
			     container (P9g; in the device backup) with zero network egress.
			     NOT 8FFB.1 (no absolute event timestamps are calculated or sent off-device),
			     NOT 3D61.1 (no user-submitted bug report carries boot time). -->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategorySystemBootTime</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>35F9.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>

	<!-- EMPTY, and that is a measured claim rather than a default. The published App Privacy label
	     (read from the ASC web console 2026-08-31) names Purchase History / User ID / Device ID —
	     all three are collected by the APP, whose manifest declares them. This extension collects
	     none of them: it makes no control-plane call at all. MorkeTunnel/ contains no URLSession
	     and no API base URL, and neither module it links (MorkeShared, WidgetKit for one
	     reloadTimelines) is used for a fetch: MorkeShared contains no URLSession either; the sing-box config reaches it through the shared Keychain, written by the app,
	     "never by a fetch from the extension" (T-CFG-41). Apple aggregates the bundles' manifests
	     into one Privacy Report, so declaring the app's three types here as well would over-state
	     what the tunnel does. -->
	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
